+# Vessel: HAVE_WSI_DRM — "the WSI can make dma-buf images" — which is not the
+# same question as "libdrm is linkable", and conflating the two is what made
+# zero-copy present silently impossible on this device.
+#
+# src/vulkan/wsi is two halves. wsi_common_x11.c's DRI3 half is gated on
+# HAVE_X11_DRM, which 'pseudo-drm' defines (patch 0004). The image backend that
+# half calls into — wsi_common_drm.c, which owns WSI_IMAGE_TYPE_DRM — was gated
+# on dep_libdrm.found() instead. For a kgsl-only Turnip, Mesa deliberately sets
+# system_has_kms_drm = false a few hundred lines above precisely so that nothing
+# links libdrm on Android, so dep_libdrm is null_dep and that file is dropped.
+#
+# The result was not a build error. get_blit_type() and configure_image() in
+# wsi_common.c put their WSI_IMAGE_TYPE_DRM cases behind #ifdef HAVE_LIBDRM and
+# end in `default: UNREACHABLE()`; with the DRM case gone, WSI_IMAGE_TYPE_CPU is
+# the only reachable label and a release compiler is entitled to drop the switch
+# and call wsi_configure_cpu_image() unconditionally. So a DRI3 swapchain got
+# CPU-linear images: no dma-buf, no modifier, and x11_image_init then dup(-1)'d
+# its way to VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY. Measured, before this:
+#     VESSEL-WSI image_init dma_buf_fd=-1 num_planes=1 modifier=0x0 row_pitch=5120
+#     VESSEL-WSI OOM x11_image_init:2733 errno=9 (Bad file descriptor)
+# which is field-for-field what wsi_create_cpu_linear_image_mem() leaves behind.
+#
+# wsi_common_drm.c does not actually need libdrm. It needs the drm-uapi headers,
+# which are in tree, plus drmIoctl and four drmDevice helpers — and Mesa already
+# ships stubs for those in src/util/libdrm.h for exactly this situation. So the
+# gate becomes "libdrm, or a pseudo-drm platform", and the file compiles against
+# the stubs when there is no libdrm to link.
+if dep_libdrm.found() or with_dri_platform == 'pseudo-drm'
+  pre_args += '-DHAVE_WSI_DRM'
+endif
+
 # Then get each libdrm module
 foreach name, d : _libdrm_checks
   if d['enabled']
--- a/src/util/libdrm.h
