+/* Vessel: drmGetDevice2() above can only fail here, so nothing can ever hold
+ * two drmDevices to compare. Answering "not equal" is the honest reading of
+ * "there are no DRM devices", and it is also the safe one: every caller uses
+ * this to decide whether two fds name the same GPU, and a false positive would
+ * have them share buffers across devices that may not be the same device.
+ */
+static inline int
+drmDevicesEqual(drmDevicePtr a, drmDevicePtr b) { return 0; }
+
